    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d5d65460_caf5b87f",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-19T19:04:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For Nuvoton, gpio_pin_get_raw() returns the pin state from the input data register.  I don\u0027t know if the input register value updates for pins that are configured as an output.  I\u0027ve seen GPIO implementations where once a pin is configured as an output, the input status is not defined.  For a warm reset, the GPIO registers should be unchanged.  Sam\u0027s experiment seems to confirm this, as the only register changes were to the GPIO input data register.",
      "parentUuid": "75624317_28414770",
      "revId": "272f0f0629beb1f46b4d8b7bd2ac10f131779fac",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a6830380_4164cf34",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000407
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-19T19:30:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But in the EC repo, it is quite common to read the input register value for a GPIO output. For example, call the function `gpio_get_level(GPIO_SOME_OUTPUT)` directly to read the status. If not doing so, the code needs to be modified to cache the output status to an extra variable.\n\nThere are many examples like checking the EN_PP5000:\n  grep -rsI EN_PP * | grep gpio_get_level\n\nIf RW skips configuring the GPIOs, this means we can\u0027t change a GPIO between INPUT and OUTPUT, between push-pull and open-drain, and between GPIO and alternative function.",
      "parentUuid": "d5d65460_caf5b87f",
      "revId": "272f0f0629beb1f46b4d8b7bd2ac10f131779fac",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
